age is a new build variant in an existing onboarded repo, so pipeline work folds into the productization epic, gated by a \"build pipeline green\" acceptance criterion rather than a separate epic or DAG edge.\n- All four strategy components exist in architecture context — no new-component onboarding chain (repo-onboarding / license-validation) is required. License scanning of the ROCm image's transitive dependencies is absorbed into the productization epic's release checklist rather than a separate epic, since the repo and its CUDA builds already ship through the same pipeline.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\n- **Tier 1 (independent value, starts immediately)**: E001 (risk-reduction validation producing the go/no-go data), E004 and E003 (training on ROCm delivers user value independent of the serving go/no-go outcome).\n- **Tier 2 (gated)**: E002 — productization is gated by the campaign outcome (E001) and scoped to the models it clears.\n- E005 (documentation) follows all implementation work per Rule 11.\n\n## Conditional Decomposition\n\nThe campaign's go/no-go outcome is a continuum (each model independently clears or fails), not a small set of distinct structural outcomes, so no branch files are generated. The gate is recorded on the productization epic as `gated_by` with `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` (scope narrows to the cleared model list; if no model clears, the epic is removed and results feed back to the strategy).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30130,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86125cd2e72d3245","agent_id":"ad4feccb015d8082a","session_id":"a1fb373b-b101-443e-9fd4-5e641a172da3","uuid":"2849418b-a9cf-49a1-b069-cd2679bad3cf","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:17:30.698Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
