{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-895b85bd-8e7f-48ad-9362-7c935ddb35b9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2026f4d730b10eb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-myskupfd/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for campaign-cleared models\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models the validation campaign clears: a midstream ROCm image build of the vLLM runtime, its productized serving runtime definition, and release through the existing build pipeline — turning the validated upstream capability into a supported platform runtime.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build and release the vLLM ROCm runtime image variant from the midstream vLLM repository, based on a published upstream ROCm release pinned for the platform release train.\n- Add the ROCm serving runtime definition (ServingRuntime) for AMD GPU nodes to the productized runtime set, scoped to the models cleared by the validation campaign.\n- Extend the existing build pipeline configuration in the already-onboarded midstream repository to build the ROCm image variant.\n- Verify integration with the serving stack: InferenceServices using the ROCm runtime deploy and serve on AMD GPU nodes through KServe with no serving control-plane code changes.\n- Record the supported-model scope, hardware, and driver prerequisites that the runtime is supported for.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The ROCm vLLM runtime image builds green in the existing build pipeline for the midstream repository.\n- A productized ServingRuntime using the ROCm image deploys InferenceServices that serve every model on the campaign's cleared list on AMD GPU nodes.\n- The runtime's supported-model scope exactly matches the go/no-go list produced by the validation campaign.\n- The shipped runtime pins a published upstream ROCm release, and the pinned version is recorded.\n- The rollout is additive and reversible: existing CUDA runtimes are unaffected, and the ROCm runtime can be disabled or removed without impacting them.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Upstream ROCm runtime image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream communities; alignment with platform release trains is an externally controlled schedule risk. Mitigated by pinning to a published upstream ROCm release (acceptance criterion above) rather than tracking a moving tag.\n- This epic is gated on the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome; its scope is rewritten to the cleared model list, and it is removed entirely if no models clear.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36127,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86125cd2e72d3245","agent_id":"ad4feccb015d8082a","session_id":"a1fb373b-b101-443e-9fd4-5e641a172da3","uuid":"0114bdc4-5e8f-4402-9fd4-9becdd1a5a37","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:17:53.958Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
