{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b595972d-53cd-4bdc-a022-33accaa73347","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a10106b3b0f455f5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-myskupfd/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E003.md","content":"# PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes PyTorch training on ROCm supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs run through the Training Operator: PyTorchJob workers schedule onto AMD Instinct GPU nodes, run with upstream PyTorch ROCm images, and are admitted through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota and gang semantics.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enable PyTorchJob worker pods to schedule onto AMD GPU nodes with `amd.com/gpu` resources (node labels/affinity and tolerations as needed for AMD-accelerated nodes).\n- Validate single-GPU PyTorchJob execution on ROCm using upstream PyTorch ROCm images.\n- Validate multi-GPU / multi-worker PyTorchJob execution on ROCm across AMD Instinct GPUs, with jobs admitted through Kueue queueing.\n- Capture any Training Operator changes or configuration required for ROCm execution, and record the validated driver, ROCm, and image versions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A single-GPU PyTorchJob runs to completion on an AMD Instinct GPU node requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources.\n- A multi-GPU, multi-worker PyTorchJob runs to completion across AMD Instinct GPUs.\n- Jobs are admitted through Kueue queueing with `amd.com/gpu` quota accounted correctly (requires the Kueue AMD GPU quota handling capability).\n- Validation is performed on AMD Instinct hardware with the driver, ROCm, and image versions recorded for reproducibility.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Validation requires access to the AMD Instinct hardware pool shared with the serving validation campaign — a coordination risk, not a dependency.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36805,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86125cd2e72d3245","agent_id":"ad4feccb015d8082a","session_id":"a1fb373b-b101-443e-9fd4-5e641a172da3","uuid":"c537d498-c2ea-4e1e-b577-df2bdcd10d99","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:18:01.942Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
