{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-030a06e7-d96c-420e-92a7-8d2af4ea5b14","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-998ff9d85cce6381","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-myskupfd/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E004.md","content":"# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for training workload admission\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers Kueue admission and quota handling for AMD GPUs so that training workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources are admitted with correct quota accounting and all-or-nothing gang semantics — the queueing foundation that PyTorch ROCm training jobs are admitted through.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the Distributed Workloads quota model to cover `amd.com/gpu` resources (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue resource flavors for AMD GPU nodes).\n- Ensure workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted with the platform's all-or-nothing semantics so multi-GPU training jobs are not partially admitted.\n- Validate quota accounting, queueing, and admission of `amd.com/gpu`-requesting workloads on a cluster with AMD GPU nodes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A workload requesting `amd.com/gpu` is admitted only when quota is available and stays pending when it is not (quota accounting is correct for the AMD GPU resource).\n- Multi-pod workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted all-or-nothing (gang semantics hold for AMD GPU jobs).\n- Quota configuration and admission behavior are validated on AMD GPU nodes with the validated setup recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Validation benefits from access to the AMD Instinct hardware pool shared with the serving validation campaign — a coordination risk, not a dependency.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reaso