{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90b924b53856553d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: -1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 3\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic makes PyTorch training on ROCm supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs run through the Training Operator: PyTorchJob workers schedule onto AMD Instinct GPU nodes, run with upstream PyTorch ROCm images, and are admitted through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota and gang semantics.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Enable PyTorchJob worker pods to schedule onto AMD GPU nodes with `amd.com/gpu` resources (node labels/affinity and tolerations as needed for AMD-accelerated nodes).\n39\t- Validate single-GPU PyTorchJob execution on ROCm using upstream PyTorch ROCm images.\n40\t- Validate multi-GPU / multi-worker PyTorchJob execution on ROCm across AMD Instinct GPUs, with jobs admitted through Kueue queueing.\n41\t- Capture any Training Operator changes or configuration required for ROCm execution, and record the validated driver, ROCm, and image versions.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob runs to completion on an AMD Instinct GPU node requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources.\n46\t- A multi-GPU, multi-worker PyTorchJob runs to completion across AMD Instinct GPUs.\n47\t- Jobs are admitted through Kueue queueing with `amd.com/gpu` quota accounted correctly (requires the Kueue AMD GPU quota handling capability).\n48\t- Validation is performed on AMD Instinct hardware with the driver, ROCm, and image versions recorded for reproducibility.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n53\t\n54\t## Risks / Notes\n55\t\n56\t- Validation requires access to the AMD Instinct hardware pool shared with the serving validation campaign — a coordination risk, not a dependency.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b1fc87e5b43481c","agent_id":"a42f09c51428f0558","session_id":"a1fb373b-b101-443e-9fd4-5e641a172da3","uuid":"f070919f-e138-46ae-8315-407ccdf7ccc0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:20:43.636Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-90b924b53856553d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
