loads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted all-or-nothing (gang semantics hold for AMD GPU jobs).\n45\t- Quota configuration and admission behavior are validated on AMD GPU nodes with the validated setup recorded.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n50\t\n51\t## Risks / Notes\n52\t\n53\t- Validation benefits from access to the AMD Instinct hardware pool shared with the serving validation campaign — a coordination risk, not a dependency.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b1fc87e5b43481c","agent_id":"a42f09c51428f0558","session_id":"a1fb373b-b101-443e-9fd4-5e641a172da3","uuid":"43d5f0ae-0d04-4225-94d4-71dd4a0df06e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:20:44.216Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab8a9ee95ad3259c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
