{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ce61f82f90ee63a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for campaign-cleared models\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: Narrow the supported-model scope to the models the validation\n15\t    campaign clears; if no models clear, remove the productization epic and feed the\n16\t    results back to the strategy.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for campaign-cleared models\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models the validation campaign clears: a midstream ROCm image build of the vLLM runtime, its productized serving runtime definition, and release through the existing build pipeline — turning the validated upstream capability into a supported platform runtime.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Build and release the vLLM ROCm runtime image variant from the midstream vLLM repository, based on a published upstream ROCm release pinned for the platform release train.\n43\t- Add the ROCm serving runtime definition (ServingRuntime) for AMD GPU nodes to the productized runtime set, scoped to the models cleared by the validation campaign.\n44\t- Extend the existing build pipeline configuration in the already-onboarded midstream repository to build the ROCm image variant.\n45\t- Verify integration with the serving stack: InferenceServices using the ROCm runtime deploy and serve on AMD GPU nodes through KServe with no serving control-plane code changes.\n46\t- Record the supported-model scope, hardware, and driver prerequisites that the runtime is supported for.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- The ROCm vLLM runtime image builds green in the existing build pipeline for the midstream repository.\n51\t- A productized ServingRuntime using the ROCm image deploys InferenceServices that serve every model on the campaign's cleared list on AMD GPU nodes.\n52\t- The runtime's supported-model scope exactly matches the go/no-go list produced by the validation campaign.\n53\t- The shipped runtime pins a published upstream ROCm release, and the pinned version is recorded.\n54\t- The rollout is additive and reversible: existing CUDA runtimes are unaffected, and the ROCm runtime can be disabled or removed without impacting them.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n59\t\n60\t## Risks / Notes\n61\t\n62\t- Upstream ROCm runtime image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream communities; alignment with platform release trains is an externally controlled schedule risk. Mitigated by pinning to a published upstream ROCm release (acceptance criterion above) rather than tracking a moving tag.\n63\t- This epic is gated on the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome; its scope is rewritten to the cleared model list, and it is removed entirely if no models clear.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa5ed1c6ebe45912","agent_id":"aba3e9d5a040feddf","session_id":"a1fb373b-b101-443e-9fd4-5e641a172da3","uuid":"9fda08dd-e765-40ee-a130-054124ed0220","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:24:05.44