{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a632357173dbd40","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for training workload admission\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: -1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for training workload admission\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers Kueue admission and quota handling for AMD GPUs so that training workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources are admitted with correct quota accounting and all-or-nothing gang semantics — the queueing foundation that PyTorch ROCm training jobs are admitted through.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Extend the Distributed Workloads quota model to cover `amd.com/gpu` resources (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue resource flavors for AMD GPU nodes).\n38\t- Ensure workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted with the platform's all-or-nothing semantics so multi-GPU training jobs are not partially admitted.\n39\t- Validate quota accounting, queueing, and admission of `amd.com/gpu`-requesting workloads on a cluster with AMD GPU nodes.\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A workload requesting `amd.com/gpu` is admitted only when quota is available and stays pending when it is not (quota accounting is correct for the AMD GPU resource).\n44\t- Multi-pod workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted all-or-nothing (gang semantics hold for AMD GPU jobs).\n45\t- Quota configuration and admission behavior are validated on AMD GPU nodes with the validated setup recorded.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n50\t\n51\t## Risks / Notes\n52\t\n53\t- Validation benefits from access to the AMD Instinct hardware pool shared with the serving validation campaign — a coordination risk, not a dependency.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa5ed1c6ebe45912","agent_id":"aba3e9d5a040feddf","session_id":"a1fb373b-b101-443e-9fd4-5e641a172da3","uuid":"eac3d215-2d79-4d2a-bcb9-8ca5b132c9e3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:24:08.702Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a632357173dbd40","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020"}
